          TESTS OF COMPOSITE DISTRIBUTIONAL HYPOTHESES FOR
          THE ANALYSIS OF BIOLOGICAL & ENVIRONMENTAL DATA

                 libcdh.a C Version 1.0 <12 Sep 1994>
        
This library contains C functions for testing the hypothesis
of normality or the hypothesis of exponentiality.  Lognormality can be
tested by carrying out the tests of normality on the log transformed
data.  Some tests are general goodness-of-fit tests that allow any
distribution to be tested simply by basing the distributional
components of the test statistic on the hypothesized distribution.  

It has been completely rewritten (by hand) from Paul Johnson's
FORTRAN version that appears in statlib. A few bugs were
fixed. Tests run faster and use less memory. Fixed limits
on sizes of input data have been removed.

From the original FORTRAN version:
